un the following command to start the tool:\n     ```bash\n     python main.py\n     ```\n\n2. **Input Query Parameters**:\n   - When prompted, input your desired query parameters, e.g., `\'cat:cs.AI\'`, to search within specific categories.\n\n3. **View or Save Results**:\n   - The tool will display the results in the console.\n   - To save the results, they will automatically be written to a CSV file named `"arxiv_results.csv"` in the current working directory.\n\n### Customizing the Tool\n- **Modify Query Parameters**: You can change the default query parameters directly in the `main.py` file if needed.\n- **Change Output File Name**: Edit the file name in the `save_results_to_csv` method call to store results under a different name.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe ArXiv Query Tool simplifies and enhances the research process by providing a streamlined way to access and manage information from the ArXiv database. With its intuitive interface and flexible functionality, researchers can efficiently gather and organize academic resources.', 'output_size': 2836, 'output_count': 1, 'output_role': 'assistant', 'output_source': 'Chief Product Officer'} Duration: 12.77332067489624
